meta {
  name: Resolve Order Lists
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/referral-lists/resolve?referralPanelId=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  referralPanelId: 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
  ~ptCategoryId: 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
  ~referredByDoctorId: 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
  ~internalReferralId: 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
  ~externalReferralId: 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  Resolve the pricing lists a Create-Order should use from the selected referrals
  / PT category. Walks the priority PANEL (B2B) → PT_CATEGORY → DOCTOR → INTERNAL
  → EXTERNAL; the first applicable configuration wins, and any unset list falls
  back to the branch's default Walk-in list — as does the whole result when
  nothing matches.

  - `referralPanelId` / `referredByDoctorId` / `internalReferralId` /
    `externalReferralId` — resolve via the branch's `ReferralListAssignment`.
  - `ptCategoryId` — priority slot 2: resolves to the PT category's mapped Lab
    Test / Lab Panel's own pricing lists (ignored if the category is inactive or
    its mappings have no list). PT category maps lab items only, so the radiology
    lists fall back to the branch defaults in that case.

  Returns `{ branchLabTestListId, branchLabPanelListId, branchRadiologyTestListId,
  branchRadiologyPanelListId, source }` where `source` is the matched referral
  type, `PT_CATEGORY`, or `DEFAULT`. Each referral maps BOTH a Lab Test / Lab
  Panel List AND a Radiology Test / Radiology Panel List; any unset list falls
  back to the branch's corresponding default Walk-in list. List ids are null only
  when the branch has never imported that catalogue (no default list yet).

  The Create-Order form feeds the radiology list ids to the branch radiology
  test/panel option pickers (`?listId=…`) so radiology items show the referral's
  prices, exactly like lab tests/panels.
}
